{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>No hand shall touch him.</b> Why is this said, when it was already said כל הנוגע? I heard from the mouth of Rabbi Yitzhak that this verse refers to what was written above, where it says כל הנוגע בהר. And this is what it says: when you come to kill the one who touched — do not touch him with your hand, but סקול יסקל — stone him from a distance, for if you go to the place where he is to kill him, you would be crossing the boundary and become liable. And it appears to me that it comes to inform us by what death you kill him — to say that he is punished by stoning, so that you should not say his death is by strangulation, as the unspecified death penalty stated in the Torah — thus it teaches us." "<b>Or shot through.</b> 'Or' is in the sense of 'if,' that is: if סקול יסקל — he should be shot through beforehand, for such is the way of those stoned, that they are pushed first and then stoned. However, it can be explained according to its plain sense: סקל יסקל — when he does not die from the push; or ירה יירה — if he dies from the push alone. And its translation: ארי אתרגמא — he shall be cast down, or אישתדאה — he shall be driven away."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:30.119556938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}